## Why This Is Asked
Tests bridging fundamentals, cross‑platform API design, and a simple, user‑visible feedback loop without heavy platform specifics.

## Key Concepts
- TurboModule/JSI bridging
- Native event emission and JSI consumption
- React hooks for native events
- Platform fallbacks (Android Vibrator vs iOS Core Haptics)
- UX implications of haptic timing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Usage sketch (React Native)
import { useLastHapticTime } from './hooks'
import { Button, Text, View } from 'react-native'

export default function HapticDemo() {
  const [ts, setTs] = useState(null)
  useEffect(() => {
    const unsub = onLastHapticTs((t) => setTs(t))
    return () => unsub()
  }, [])
  return (
    <View>
      <Button title="Pulse Haptic" onPress={() => startHaptic([20,40,20])} />
      <Text>Last haptic: {ts ?? 'none'}</Text>
    </View>
  )
}
```

